# TUI-DESIGN-4 §10 / §13 — the round-4 live leg. A zero-argument `jevcode` against live Jev through TypeSafe native
# (JEV_PROVIDER auto → typesafe from TYPESAFE_API_KEY in the repository's ./.env), the generator key unset in the
# environment (`env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`), a temp JEVCODE_HOME, the workspace a fresh copy of examples/demo-py
# (git init, .venv with pytest). Reviews are answered by the driver (PTY_AUTO_REVIEW=y). Every pause is a draining
# `sleep` (research 20 §5). Every run-frame anchor is round 4's and glyph-agnostic (§3.6 G1, `[·-]`).
expect \x1b\[\?25l
mark first-frame
expect step 0/
expect \x1b\[\?2004h
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
mark composer-ready
# the splash settles by itself into the version caption (§5.2 row 14)
expect ◆(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*\d+\.\d+\.\d+
mark splash-settled
sleep 0.3
# a greeting: one Jev intake request, a [you] bubble, a [jevcode] reply, no run
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
mark hi-sent
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*hi
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
mark hi-reply
sleep 0.5
# §3.1 the kv block grammar, live: /jev before any run
send /jev
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect intake {2,}1 message
mark jev-before-run
sleep 0.3
# a real task under the llm-jev default: the §3.6 run frame, the §6 review card if one appears (PTY_AUTO_REVIEW)
send Fix the failing tests in tests/test_core.py without changing the tests.
sleep 0.3
send \r
mark task-sent
expect \[run\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*started [·-] 
mark run-started
expect \[step 1\]
mark step-1
expect finished [·-] (complete|max_steps|spend_cap|wall_time|human_pause|replan_stop|impossible|error)
mark run-ended
sleep 0.5
# §3.6/§3.7's history rows and the §3.1 blocks after a run
send /cost
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect chat {2,}\$
mark cost-shown
sleep 0.3
send /status
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[ui\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*status
mark status-shown
sleep 0.3
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
